# Corpus unit sapg/C02 — gap (unmet-mandatory-CQ path: baseline parity)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/sapg.yaml C02 (comparative, controlled_comparison; corpus pin 62e9b54).
# Headline: SAPG achieves significantly higher asymptotic performance than PPO, DexPBT, and PQL
# on hard dexterous manipulation tasks — up to 12-66% over DexPBT on the AllegroKuka hard suite
# at 2e10 steps, with PPO and PQL near-zero; all methods run at N=24,576 envs, 16-step horizon,
# 5 seeds (E02 / E03, Table 1 / Figure 5).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Three baselines; nearest-competitor / binding-conjunct convention takes DexPBT as B (the
#     toughest comparand, matched population size M=6, beaten by 12-66%). PPO and PQL, which fail
#     entirely on the hard suite, stay in nl and the premise leaf refs.
#   * The mandatory baseline_parity CQ is unmet, so no complete controlled_comparison is
#     declarable (E2-style gap). Annotation CQ "were the baselines given equivalent tuning effort
#     or their authors' recommended hyperparameters?" is mandatory unmet-gap — E02 fixes SAPG's
#     configuration in detail but specifies only population structure for DexPBT and nothing for
#     PPO/PQL tuning. The met "same env count / horizon / step budget" CQ1 is a facet of matched
#     setup but does not cover baseline configuration, so it is folded into the premise refs and
#     baseline_parity stays undischarged.
#   * measurement_validity and variance_reported ARE met: the metric (episode successes at 2e10
#     steps) is computed identically for all methods, and annotation CQ "is seed-level
#     uncertainty reported?" gives mean +- standard error over 5 seeds. The optional
#     parameter/compute-parity CQ is unmet-gap and omitted (optional, no status effect).
#   * Same shape as adaptive-pruning/C03 (comparative controlled_comparison landing gap), here
#     through baseline_parity rather than variance_reported.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact sapg at sha256:f4108aa329a9
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar ---------------

claim c02
  nl      = "SAPG achieves significantly higher asymptotic performance than DexPBT (by 12 to 66 percent) on the hard AllegroKuka dexterous manipulation suite at 2e10 steps, with PPO and PQL near-zero on the same tasks; all methods run at N=24576 envs, 16-step horizon, 5 seeds with mean +- stderr"
  formal  = better(sapg, dexpbt, asymptotic_success, allegro_kuka_hard)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the E02 per-(method, task) success cells (Table 1 / Figure 5), with the
# shared N=24,576 / 2e10-step conditions folded into refs per result cell.
leaf e1 : reports(e02, compares(sapg, dexpbt, asymptotic_success, allegro_kuka_hard, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C02, logic/experiments.md#E02, Table-1, Figure-5, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N12]

leaf e2 : valid_measurement(asymptotic_success, e02)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-step-6]

leaf e3 : variance_reported(e02)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-step-6]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: matched_setup(sapg, dexpbt, e02) is unmet — PPO/PQL tuning is
# unstated and only DexPBT's population structure is fixed — and baseline_parity is mandatory,
# so the claim's complete-support set is empty.)

status c02

